            <profile id="0083-c048-9f0e-8381" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, shield and heavy armour. May ride a warhorse (free). May have partial plate armour (free if mounted, +2 pts if on foot). Mounted Commanders may have a lance (+4 pts) and cloth barding (+4 pts) for their mounts. Commanders on foot may have halberd (+3 pts) or double-handed weapon (+4 pts). Later Army options: full plate armour (free if mounted, +4 pts if on foot) and plate barding (+6 pts). One Commander may be upgraded to Army General (+35 pts, +1 Wound); one other Commander may be upgraded to Army Standard Bearer (+15 pts), who may not upgrade equipment except for a warhorse and partial plate armour. Any unit led by a Clerical Commander is immune to panic as long as he is alive and with the unit. (Armies of Chivalry p.41)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="6392-26da-e596-1d02" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">4+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
