            </profile>
            <profile id="7f51-7b5b-2e96-7767" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, heavy armour and shield, lance and warhorse. May take cloth barding (+4 pts) and partial plate armour (free, shield optional). Later Army: full plate armour (free if mounted) and plate barding (+6 pts). One unit of Ritter may be Stubborn (+3 pts) and must be led by the Army General. Combined Formation; Ritter may combine with Ministerialen, who are placed in the rear ranks. In Early Armies mounted Ritter have First Charge, are Impetuous and may count their Rank Bonus up to +1. In Later Armies mounted Ritter may count a Rank Bonus of up to +2. 0-2 Ritter units (mounted and dismounted together; entered as 0-2 each). (Armies of Chivalry p.41)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="c842-4ae3-c09e-450b" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">3+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
