            <profile id="62eb-edd1-b8f9-1e7e" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, thrusting spear and shield. May have light armour (+1 pt) or heavy armour (+2 pts). Later Army options: halberd instead of spear (+1 pt), or pike instead of spear &amp; shield (+1 pt); partial plate armour (+3 pts). May be in Mixed Order units with Crossbowmen, Archers or Handgunners of the same type. Pikemen fight in a Medieval Phalanx and may not be in Mixed Order units. Later Imperial Armies: mercenaries that fight on foot count as Landsknecht (+1 pt per model up to 20 pts per unit); for every unit of Landsknecht Pikemen, a unit of eight Landsknecht Halberdier or Handgunner models may be upgraded to Verlorene Haufe (+1 pt per model). (Armies of Chivalry p.41)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="59ff-1dd8-4e8e-c90e" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="5+">
