            <profile id="63ec-9341-bfc1-28d0" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and bow. May take crossbow or handgun instead of bow (+2 pts). May have light armour (+1 pt). Later Army options: crossbowmen and handgunners may have heavy armour (+2 pts) and pavise (+2 pts). Open Order or Mixed Order with Spearmen or Halberdiers of the same type. For each Crossbowman model at least two Spearmen, Pikemen or Halberdier models must be taken. City armies: Militia may be upgraded to WS3 &amp; BS3 (+1 pt per model). (Armies of Chivalry p.41)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="6b60-77e4-08ab-251f" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="6+">
                <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="031f-b2bd-a062-ab61" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="f989-24ca-9cb1-c37f" type="atLeast"/>
