            </profile>
            <profile id="4070-092c-607f-86a8" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">The cost of the war wagon includes six crewmen: three armed with halberds and three with crossbow or handgun, all with light armour. A team of 2-4 horses. War wagons may be single models (no Leader, Standard Bearer or Musician) or grouped in units of at least three models. One wagon per unit may include a tarasnices (palisade gun) for +20 pts (not built). Later Feudal or Clerical armies: 0-1 War Wagon. (Armies of Chivalry p.41)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="2d24-987a-31c4-2d8f" name="War Wagon (Chivalry)" hidden="false" targetId="3e37-dc67-7f91-7046" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="120"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
