  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="ca59-2510-ce9e-ccce" name="Holy Roman Empire (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>THE HOLY ROMAN EMPIRE 1254-1519 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.40-41). Choose Early (1254-1438) or Later (1438-1519) and the type of the Army General (Imperial, Feudal, Clerical or City) in the Army composition list. Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 15-33%, Infantry 25-50% (Early) or 25-33% (Later), Mercenaries 25-50% (Early) or 25-75% (Later). In this catalogue the Mercenary versions of troops, the Allied or Mercenary Knights and the Mercenary Diener count against the Mercenaries allocation; Ritter, Ministerialen and Militia Diener count as Cavalry; Militia, Levies, artillery and wagons count as Infantry. Verlorene Haufe (Lost Bunch): for every unit of Landsknecht Pikemen, a unit of eight Landsknecht Halberdier or Handgunner models may be upgraded to Verlorene Haufe (+1 pt per model). They are Skirmishers and may re-roll their first failed Panic test; each unit must be attached to a parent unit of Landsknecht Pikemen at the start of the battle and stay within 6" of it or lose the re-roll. Only in Later Imperial armies. Allies &amp; Mercenaries: unless stated otherwise all Allied &amp; Mercenary troops in this list and troops drawn from other lists are subject to the Allies &amp; Mercenaries rule. Mercenary units led by a Commander, the Army General or the Army Standard Bearer are not subject to it. Any unit led by a Clerical Commander is immune to panic as long as he is alive and with the unit.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Holy Roman Empire - Early Imperial]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%, at least 15%
  Infantry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Early Imperial Army (1254-1438). If an Imperial Army General is chosen and the army includes less than three Militia units, either 0-2 units from the English HYW list, or 0-2 Communal troops from the Low Countries list, or 0-1 unit from the Teutonic Order list may be chosen as additional Mercenaries (documented only).
[Holy Roman Empire - Early Feudal]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%, at least 15%
  Infantry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Early Feudal Army (1254-1438). If a Feudal Army General is chosen, the army may include either 0-2 units of Hungarian Light Cavalry from the Kingdom of Hungary list, or 0-2 Communal troops from the Low Countries list (documented only).
[Holy Roman Empire - Early Clerical]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%, at least 15%
  Infantry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Early Clerical Army (1254-1438). If a Clerical Army General is chosen, the army may include either 0-2 units of Hungarian Light Cavalry from the Kingdom of Hungary list, or 0-2 Communal troops from the Low Countries list (documented only). If no Army Standard Bearer is chosen a Carrocio may be taken.
[Holy Roman Empire - Early City]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%, at least 15%
  Infantry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Early City Army (1254-1438). If a City Army General is chosen, any Militia unit may be upgraded to WS3 &amp; BS3 (+1 pt per model). 0-2 Mercenary units from this list may be chosen. If no Army Standard Bearer is chosen a Carrocio may be taken.
[Holy Roman Empire - Later Imperial]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%, at least 15%
  Infantry: up to 33%, at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Later Imperial Army (1438-1519). If an Imperial Army General is chosen, only 0-2 Militia units may be chosen. All Mercenaries from this list that fight on foot count as Landsknecht (+1 pt per model up to a maximum points cost of 20 pts per unit). Landsknecht do not roll to test their loyalty at the beginning of the battle like other Allies &amp; Mercenaries, but still cannot use the benefits of the Army General or the Army Standard Bearer. Later Imperial armies may draw on 0-1 unit from the Teutonic Order list, and 0-2 units of Pikemen from the Low Countries or the Swiss lists (documented only).
[Holy Roman Empire - Later Feudal]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%, at least 15%
  Infantry: up to 33%, at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Later Feudal Army (1438-1519). Only 0-2 Militia or Levy units may be chosen. 0-1 War Wagon may be chosen.
[Holy Roman Empire - Later Clerical]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%, at least 15%
  Infantry: up to 33%, at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Later Clerical Army (1438-1519). Only 0-2 Militia or Levy units may be chosen. 0-1 War Wagon may be chosen.
[Holy Roman Empire - Later City]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%, at least 15%
  Infantry: up to 33%, at least 25%
  Mercenaries: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Later City Army (1438-1519). If a City Army General is chosen, every other Militia unit may be upgraded to WS3 &amp; BS3 (+1 pt per model). 0-3 Mercenary units from this list may be chosen. Levies may not be chosen. If at least 33% of the available points have been spent on Militia troops, a Wagon Tabor may be chosen (1 Wagon per 500 army points), paid out of the Infantry points allowance.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
